intent: >
  Fix the two bootstrap rough edges the VM run exposed: non-interactive prompt-abort
  and the missing zsh login-shell, so a fresh machine is actually ready to work.
slice: "verification/bootstrap-polish"
kind: fix
behavior_change: additive
reversibility: reversible
scope:
  declared: [script/bootstrap]
  actual: [script/bootstrap]
  drift: []
proof:
  tests_run: "bash -n + shellcheck script/bootstrap; VM: guard non-interactive skip test + sudo chsh shell-change test"
  result: green
  failing: 0
tests:
  needed: "no"
  rationale: >
    Verified on the Ubuntu VM: `[ -t 0 ]` reports non-interactive (setup skipped) under
    limactl shell, and the chsh block changes the login shell /bin/bash -> /usr/bin/zsh
    via sudo (no password prompt). bash -n clean; shellcheck adds no new findings (the
    SC2059/SC2166/etc. are pre-existing in untouched helpers/link_file).
verification:
  tested:
    - "Guard: [ -t 0 ] false in non-interactive run -> setup_gitconfig_local skipped"
    - "chsh: getent passwd shows /usr/bin/zsh after the block"
  manual:
    - "Interactive path (real TTY prompts) unchanged — not re-walked; only the guard condition changed"
specifications:
  - "Interactive git/SSH setup runs only when stdin is a real terminal ([ -t 0 ])"
  - "zsh is set as the login shell via sudo chsh when not already zsh; macOS no-ops; failure is non-fatal"
assumptions:
  - "sudo is available (bootstrap/dot already require it) so `sudo chsh` needs no password"
  - "zsh is installed before this point — true: the package step / bin/dot installs it on Linux"
deviations_from_plan: >
  "Polish beyond the original plan, from the VM run. Chose auto-chsh (sudo) over
  document-only for the 'ready to work' goal; guarded + reversible. Lands on PR 1
  (#10), bootstrap's home PR — standalone branch, no rebase cascade."
trade_offs: >
  "Auto-chsh changes the user's login shell (significant but exactly the ready-to-work
  intent; reversible via chsh). Used sudo chsh so it works non-interactively; the cost
  is it acts without a per-user confirmation, mitigated by the not-already-zsh guard."
self_review:
  consistency: "Uses the existing success() helper and sudo pattern; guard is a standard `[ -t 0 ]`."
  error_paths: "chsh wrapped in if/else (non-fatal); /etc/shells append has || true; guard prevents redundant runs."
  security: "sudo chsh + appending zsh to /etc/shells are standard; no new secret handling."
  api: "bootstrap behavior change: now sets login shell. No interface/caller change."
confidence: high
reviewer_attention:
  - "script/bootstrap: the sudo chsh block — confirm you want auto-change-login-shell (vs documenting it)"
